# FiTuna run artifacts
*.gguf
*.gguf.tmp
out/
.fituna_cache.sqlite3

# `fituna fetch-corpus` output: a downloaded corpus, not a project source
# (see README Quickstart step 3) -- covers any --out path, not just the two
# example filenames, since the tool lets users pick any name ending in .txt.
# Also covers its atomic-write temp file, always named `.<out-name>.<random
# suffix>.tmp` next to the destination regardless of --out name (see
# tempfile.mkstemp() in fituna/corpus.py's fetch_corpus()).
*.txt
.*.tmp

